			"description": "<ul><li>This is the core feature allowing users to design the chatbot's conversational capabilities through a low-code admin interface</li><li>- <strong>Intents</strong>: Users define 'intents' which represent a user's goal, such as 'check_order_status'</li><li>Each intent has a unique ID and a speech response</li><li>- <strong>Entities</strong>: Users create custom 'entities' to extract specific pieces of information from user input, like an 'order_number'</li><li>- <strong>Parameters</strong>: Intents are configured with parameters that map to entities</li><li>The system can prompt the user if a required parameter is missing, enabling multi-turn dialogues</li><li>- <strong>Implementation</strong>: The frontend (<code>/admin/intents/page</li><li>tsx</code>, <code>/admin/entities/page</li><li>tsx</code>) interacts with backend REST APIs (<code>/app/admin/intents/routes</li><li>py</code>, <code>/app/admin/entities/routes</li><li>py</code>) to manage these configurations in the database</li></ul>",
