			],
			"description": "<ul><li>This feature enables the chatbot to understand natural language by training Machine Learning models on user-provided examples</li><li>- <strong>Provide Examples</strong>: Users input various example sentences for each intent to teach the bot different ways a user might express a goal</li><li>- <strong>Annotate Entities</strong>: Through the UI (<code>/frontend/app/admin/intents/id/train/page</li><li>tsx</code>), users can highlight and label entities within the training sentences</li><li>- <strong>Model Training</strong>: The system uses this labeled data to train an intent classification model (<code>SklearnIntentClassifier</code>) and an entity extraction model (<code>CRFEntityExtractor</code>)</li><li>- <strong>NLU Pipeline</strong>: These trained models become components of the NLU pipeline (<code>/app/bot/nlu/pipeline</li><li>py</code>) which processes all incoming user messages</li></ul>",
