					"outputDataExample": "{\"thread_id\": \"user_session_123\", \"bot_message\": [{\"text\": \"Your order status is <b>Shipped</b> and is expected to arrive in 2-3 business days.\"}], \"complete\": true, ...}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>This powerful feature allows the chatbot to connect to external services to fetch data or perform actions, making it truly functional</li><li>- <strong>API Trigger</strong>: Intents can be configured to trigger a REST API call once all required parameters have been collected from the user</li><li>- <strong>Dynamic Payloads</strong>: The API URL, headers, and request body can be dynamically constructed using Jinja2 templates, inserting the values of extracted parameters</li><li>- <strong>Dynamic Responses</strong>: The chatbot's final response can also be templated to include data returned from the API call, providing dynamic and personalized information</li><li>- <strong>Core Logic</strong>: This is handled within the <code>DialogueManager</code> (<code>_handle_api_trigger</code> and <code>_call_intent_api</code> methods), as demonstrated in the <code>docs/03-creating-order-status-check</li><li>md</code> example</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
